# The Edge deploy payload is fingerprinted by sha256 over its exact bytes
# (tools/pack-edge.mjs -> payload-hash.js -> the deployed GET -> the smoke guard).
# With core.autocrlf=true a Windows worktree hands the packer CRLF while a Linux
# checkout hands it LF, so the SAME COMMIT packs to two different hashes and the
# guard fails on whichever machine did not do the deploy. Pin every file that
# feeds that payload to LF so the fingerprint is a property of the commit.
supabase/functions/** text eol=lf
src/core/** text eol=lf
src/data/** text eol=lf

# Migrations and SQL fixtures are READ OFF DISK AS TEXT by the test harnesses
# (tests/raid-band-denial.mjs, tests/market-offers-guard.mjs,
# tests/conservation-fuzz.mjs), which locate anchor strings in them to plant
# mutations and to truncate at a commit-gate banner. Those anchors are authored
# with LF. On a CRLF checkout they match NOTHING, and the harness degrades to
# running zero mutations — b330 hit exactly this: four of five mutations
# reported "anchor text is not in the migration -- the mutation is decoration".
# It failed LOUDLY, which is the only reason it was caught. Pin them to LF so a
# falsifiability check cannot be silently disarmed by a line ending.
supabase/migrations/** text eol=lf
tests/sql/** text eol=lf
